reports and a literature review</article-title><source>Br Dent J</source><year>2005</year><volume>199</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>269</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16155536</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="book"><source>Antenatal care in developing countries: promises, achievements and missed opportunities</source><year>2003</year><publisher-name> Geneva, World Health Organisation</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fitzgerald</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Behets</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Preval</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal></etal></person-group><article-title>Decreased congenital syphilis incidence in Haiti rural artibonite region following decentralized prenatal screening</article-title><source>Am J Pub Health</source><year>2003</year><volume>93</volume><fpage>444</fpage><lpage>446</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12604493</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>